🔶 1. Shifted String Match (String Manipulation, HashMap)

Given two strings A and B, return true if B can be formed by shifting characters of A to the right any number of times.

Example:
A = "abcde", B = "cdeab" → true

{{Deutsche_Bank_String_Manipulation.java}}

🔶 2. Smallest Sum ≥ Target with Two Numbers (Two Pointers)

Given an array and integer T, find two numbers whose product is ≥ T but whose sum is minimum possible.

Return that minimum sum.

🔶 3. Scatter Palindrome Count (Popular in Banks)

Given a string, count how many substrings can be rearranged to form a palindrome.

🔶 4. Buy Candles Simulation (Stack Simulation)

You get a stack of candles with different heights.
You have queries: buy the topmost candle whose height ≥ X.
When bought, the candle is removed.

Return which candles you bought.

🔶 5. Monster vs Heroes Power Match (Greedy / Sorting)

You have monsters and heroes arrays.
A hero can kill a monster if heroPower ≥ monsterPower.
Find the minimum number of heroes required to defeat all monsters.

🔶 6. Minimum UI Components (Greedy + Sorting)

Given N rectangular UI boxes, minimize the number of rows needed so width per row ≤ W.

🔶 7. Minimum Time to Finish Jobs (Binary Search on Answer)

Given array of job times and K workers, find minimum time to finish all jobs if each worker must do consecutive jobs.

🔶 8. Koko-style Banana Eating Problem (Binary Search)

Classic: Find minimum integer X such that Koko finishes piles within H hours.

🔶 9. Balanced Substring with Equal 0s and 1s (Prefix / HashMap)

Given a binary string, return longest substring with equal 0s and 1s.

🔶 10. Currency Exchange Rates (Graph + BFS)

Given exchange rates as edges, find best conversion rate from currency A to B.

🔶 11. Validate Credit Card (Simulation)

Given a card number string, validate using Luhn Algorithm.

🔶 12. Minimum Window of Unique Values (Sliding Window)

Given an array, return minimum window size containing all distinct values in the array.

🔶 13. Candidate Filter System (Map + Custom Sorting)

Given list of candidates with name, score, experience, sort by:

Highest score

Highest experience

Alphabetical

Return final sorted list.

🔶 14. Longest Increasing Difficulty Tasks (DP)

Given task difficulty array, find length of LIS (Longest Increasing Subsequence).

🔶 15. Online Bank Account (Simulation)

Operations:

"deposit X"

"withdraw X"

"charge X" (cannot go below 0)

Return final account balance.